  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have\n\n$$\n(7x)\\times (3{x}^{2})=21{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* a binomial (it's a monomial).\n\n- Statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n(4x)\\times (5)=20x,\n$$\n\nwhich is a monomial.\n\n- Statement III is false. There are products of two monomials that are not binomials (see, for example, statement I and II).\n\nIn fact, the product of two monomials is *never* a binomial.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
